                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 7,1863.—At 1.30 p.m. we were boarded by a
                    government pilot, who took charge, and at 1.45 p.m. they brought the ship into
                    the harbor of Key West—myself and passengers detained on board. Captain Lewis
                    and pilot left the ship. I then sent a note to her Britannic Majesty’s
                    consul.</p>
                <p rendition="#right">STEPHEN JARMAN, <hi rendition="#italic">Master.</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#right">H. BOND, <hi rendition="#italic">Mate.</hi></p>
                <p>Witnesses: Samuel J. Redgate, Lloyd’s agent, Matamoras, G. W. Almond, Robert
                    Bowdon, F. Mohl, P. J. Edwards, John H. Ellsworth, Theod. Heych.</p>
            </div>
